INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(25076, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The bat fought you every moment of it, did it not?  Good.  A hunter who has never bled for a pet does not deserve one.$b$bThere is more to learn.', 0),
(25077, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Even the plague could not rob that beast of its strength, and for a time that strength was yours.  Remember the feeling.$b$bOne test remains before you may tame a beast without the rod.', 0),
(25078, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There is nothing left for me to teach you for now, $n.  You have fought beside bat, bear and hound, and you know what it is to command those you once hunted.$b$bI grant you the power to tame a beast of your own, to call it and to dismiss it.  Choose a companion that suits the hunt you mean to lead.', 0),
(26100, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A boar will follow anyone who feeds it, they say.  Now you know how much truth there is in that.$b$bReady for something with claws?', 0),
(26101, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Strong, patient, and hungry all day long - now you know the bear.$b$bOne lesson is left before I let you choose a companion of your own.', 0),
(26102, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, $n.  You have fought beside a boar, a bear and a wolf, and you know now that a beast is a companion, not a tool.$b$bI will give you the skills to tame a beast of your own choosing, to call it to your side and to dismiss it.  Choose well.', 0),
(25083, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So Dedlow has sent me another one.$b$b<Apolos looks you over.>$b$bYou will serve the Dark Lady well with what you have learned.  Give me a moment to show you how to train your pet, how to keep it fed and how to bring it back when it falls, and you can be on your way.$b$bOne thing more.  There are curious gargoyles perched on the Ruins of Lordaeron, right above our heads.  The living cannot tame such things; we can.  Practice your new skill on them!', 0),
(26103, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A new hunter, and one of our own for a change - most who come to me have walked all the way from Ironforge.$b$bYes, I can teach you what you need to train and guide your pet.  You will be able to teach it new abilities, to feed it, and to revive it should it fall in battle.$b$bRespect your pet and treat it well, $n, and it will be the most loyal friend you ever had.$b$bOh, and we have a fine kennel near Goldshire, by Crystal Lake.  Drop by sometime!', 0);
-- Karrina Mekenda now ends a quest
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `npcflag` = `npcflag` | 2 WHERE `entry` = 2879;

-- The first class quest: a letter from the hunter trainer of the starting place (pattern: dwarf hunters' 3108).
--   26104 Etched Letter: 197 -> 43278, after quest 7
--   26105 Etched Scroll: 1569 -> 38911, after quest 364
DELETE FROM `page_text` WHERE `ID` IN (60203, 60204);
INSERT INTO `page_text` (`ID`, `Text`, `NextPageID`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(60203, 'Word travels fast in a valley this small, $N, and it tells me a new hunter has come to Northshire. Good. Stormwind has knights and mages enough; what it lacks is eyes in the forest and a steady hand on a gun.$B$BWhen you have found your feet, come and see me. I keep my wolves outside the Abbey walls, a little way from the doors - you will hear them before you see me.$B$BAshley Blank, Hunter Trainer', 0, 0),
(60204, 'So you clawed your way out of the grave with a hunter''s instincts intact, $N. That is rarer than you think; most of us wake remembering nothing but hunger.$B$BThe Dark Lady has need of those who can track, stalk and kill from a distance. Find me in Deathknell when you are done with the errands they give you. Pavlova will smell you coming.$B$BXavier the Huntsman', 0, 0);
